import javax.swing.*;
import java.awt.*;
public class FlowDemo {
public static void main(String[] args) {
JFrame f = new JFrame("FlowLayout");
f.setLayout(new FlowLayout());
String[] b = { "New", "Open", "Save", "Print", "Exit" };
for (String s : b)
f.add(new JButton(s));
f.setSize(300, 120);
f.setDefaultCloseOperation(JFrame.EXIT_ON_CLOSE);
f.setVisible(true);
}
}
Output:
BorderDemo : NORTH across the top, SOUTH across the bottom,
WEST and EAST at the sides, CENTER fills the middle.
Enlarge the window - only CENTER grows.
GridDemo : twelve equal keys in four rows of three.
FlowDemo : five buttons in a row; narrow the window and
they wrap onto a second row.
